{
  "description": "Deterministic resolution vectors for price_adjustments on binding fixed-price pricing options. Two row kinds: index rows (kind index, a multiplicative factor compounded in declared order) and premium rows (kind fee or discount, a rate of the indexed price or a fixed amount, added). Indexed price = base x product of firing factors; resolved price = indexed price + premium deltas. Selection rows fire at most once per dimension (the first valid matching row in declared order); always rows fire independently; valid_from/valid_until bound a row to a half-open window evaluated at the purchase start_time, and a flight that crosses a window boundary of a row that would otherwise apply is rejected. Each index step applies its delta (running +/- round half away from zero of running x |factor-1|) at price precision (greatest of the currency minor-unit exponent, 4 for cpm/vcpm/cpc/cpcv/cpv/cpp, and the fewest decimals that exactly represent fixed_price and each amount, by numeric value); each premium rate delta is rounded the same way against the indexed price; the resolved price is the exact sum and never below zero. Arithmetic MUST be exact decimal or integer. Each fired row is recorded in price_breakdown: an index as a fee or discount rate, a premium as its currency amount.",
  "currency_minor_unit_exponent": {
    "USD": 2,
    "JPY": 0,
    "EUR": 2
  },
